«
@@ ============================================================
@@ ΔRf — interval arithmetic for a composite function of one
@@ variable: the range of f over an interval.
@@
@@ Input:  'f(x)' X, where f is an expression of the name x, and X
@@         an interval a…b, a±b or a±p%, with or without units.
@@ Output: the smallest and largest values of f over X, as an
@@         interval of the same form as X (a±p% gives a±b).
@@ Unlike evaluating f on X directly, the variable is counted once,
@@ however often it appears: '(x-1)·(x-2)·(x-3)' on 2±1 gives
@@ -0.385…0.385, not -4…4.
@@ Method: f is evaluated at 65 points spread over X, ends
@@ included; each local maximum or minimum of these values is
@@ refined by a golden section search, and the result is the
@@ smallest and the largest of all the candidates. An extremum
@@ narrower than 1/64 of X may be missed: Exmnf draws f to check.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================

  → fx xv
  «
    @ The bounds lo and hi of X, with its unit
    1 xv
    If xv TypeName "unit" == Then Drop Drop 1 xv →Unit xv UVal End
    Dup TypeName
    → un iv tn
    «
      Case
        tn "range" == Then iv Explode End
        tn "drange" == Then iv Explode → cv dv « cv dv - cv dv + » End
        tn "prange" == Then
          iv Explode → cv pv « cv Abs pv * 100 / → dv « cv dv - cv dv + » »
        End
        tn "uncertain" == Then
          "ΔRf works on bounds; use σRf for a±σb" DoError
        End
        iv iv
      End
      un * Swap un * Swap

      → lo hi
      «
        @ f at one point x is written out each time: a program kept in a
        @ local variable would recall the wrong local from a deeper block
        hi lo - 64 /
        → hs
        «
          @ The 65 values of f
          0 64 For kk lo kk hs * + { x 0 } 2 Rot Put 'fx' Rcl Swap Where →Num Next
          65 →List
          → ys
          «
            @ Candidates: both ends, and the refined local extrema
            ys 1 Get ys 65 Get 2 →List
            → cds
            «
              2 64 For kk
                ys kk Get
                → yk
                «
                  @ +1 for a local maximum, -1 for a local minimum
                  0
                  If yk ys kk 1 - Get ≥ yk ys kk 1 + Get ≥ And Then Drop 1 End
                  If yk ys kk 1 - Get ≤ yk ys kk 1 + Get ≤ And Then Drop -1 End
                  → sg
                  «
                    If sg 0 ≠ Then
                      @ Golden section search for the extremum of sg·f
                      lo kk 2 - hs * + lo kk hs * +
                      → xa xb
                      «
                        1 60 Start
                          xb xb xa - 0.618033988749895 * -
                          xa xb xa - 0.618033988749895 * +
                          → gx gd
                          «
                            If gx { x 0 } 2 Rot Put 'fx' Rcl Swap Where →Num sg * gd { x 0 } 2 Rot Put 'fx' Rcl Swap Where →Num sg * > Then
                              gd 'xb' Store
                            Else
                              gx 'xa' Store
                            End
                          »
                        Next
                        xa xb + 2 / { x 0 } 2 Rot Put 'fx' Rcl Swap Where →Num
                      »
                      cds Swap + yk + 'cds' Store
                    End
                  »
                »
              Next

              @ The smallest and largest candidates
              cds Sort
              → srt
              «
                srt 1 Get srt srt Size Get
                → rmn rmx
                «
                  If rmn TypeName "unit" == Then
                    1 rmn →Unit
                    → uf
                    «
                      rmn UVal rmx uf Convert UVal
                      If tn "range" == Then →Range Else
                        → yl yh « yl yh + 2 / yh yl - 2 / →∆Range »
                      End
                      uf →Unit
                    »
                  Else
                    rmn rmx
                    If tn "range" == Then →Range Else
                      → yl yh « yl yh + 2 / yh yl - 2 / →∆Range »
                    End
                  End
                »
              »
            »
          »
        »
      »
    »
  »
»
